config USB_BST_VIRT_DEVICE
      tristate "Virtual USB host device driver"
      depends on USB_BST_VIRT_MSG
      help
          This option enables the building of the Virtual USB host device driver,
          which provides support for a virtual USB device over the msgbox interface.
          If you have a system that uses a virtual USB device for communication,
          you should select this option. It will also automatically select the
          necessary Virtual USB msgbox driver if it is not already selected,
          ensuring the proper interaction between the host device and the msgbox system.

config USB_BST_VIRT_MSG
       tristate "Virtual USB msgbox driver"
       help
           The Virtual USB msgbox driver provides a communication interface for
           virtual USB devices. This driver is necessary for systems that
           implement a message-based communication mechanism over USB, allowing
           for efficient data transfer and device management.

           If you have a device that requires the Virtual USB msgbox driver for
           proper operation, you should select this option. It will be built
           into the kernel if you choose M or Y. If you are unsure, selecting
           N is safe, but your device may not function correctly without this driver.

           Note that this driver is automatically selected when the Virtual USB
           host device driver is enabled, ensuring that both components are
           available for systems that require them.